TensorFlow's repository rules (third_party/repo.bzl and XLA's copy) run
patch_cmds as ctx.execute(["bash", "-c", cmd]). On Windows CreateProcess
looks in System32 before PATH, so on a GitHub runner `bash` is the WSL
launcher, which has no distribution: the fetch of build_bazel_rules_android
fails with an empty stderr (its output is UTF-16 "Windows Subsystem for Linux
has no installed distributions"). From LiteRT-LM v0.20.0 libLiteRt and the
WebGPU accelerator build from LiteRT's source and fetch it. This runs the
shell BAZEL_SH names when it is set (the Windows workflows set Git's bash)
and plain `bash` otherwise, as before. Strip 0, like
third_party/tensorflow/tensorflow.patch. Against TensorFlow
faa06da43657488c1f7479289d11d15e03a15ba1 (LiteRT-LM v0.20.0 TENSORFLOW_REF).

diff --git a/third_party/repo.bzl b/third_party/repo.bzl
--- third_party/repo.bzl
+++ third_party/repo.bzl
@@ -83,7 +83,7 @@
                     ctx.patch(patch_file, strip = 1)
 
         for cmd in ctx.attr.patch_cmds:
-            res = ctx.execute(["bash", "-c", cmd])
+            res = ctx.execute([ctx.os.environ.get("BAZEL_SH", "bash"), "-c", cmd])
             if res.return_code != 0:
                 fail("patch_cmds failed: %s\n%s" % (cmd, res.stderr))
 
